Definitions
- "Derivative Work": Any work that includes, incorporates, or is derived from the Software,
whether modified or unmodified, including source‑code and binary distributions.
NOTE: Software that merely invokes the public API of the Software without copying, modifying,
or incorporating any source code of the Software shall NOT be considered a Derivative Work.
- "Closed‑source derivative work": A derivative work where the complete source code is
not made publicly available to recipients.
- "Valid source line": A line containing executable source code logic. Blank lines, line breaks,
whitespace‑only indentation adjustments, comments, and annotation lines shall NOT be counted
as valid source lines.
- "Commercial activity": Any activity intended to generate direct or indirect monetary gain,
including but not limited to: charging fees for access, paid subscriptions, paid features,
in‑app advertising, paid consulting services, paid hosting services.
Exclusions: voluntary donations (no obligation to provide premium benefits in return),
official project promotion, creation and distribution of official development documentation.
- "Original unmodified source file": The exact source file published by the original author,
without any edits.

1. No individual or entity may defame, slander, or disparage the original author
or the original project in any form, including public statements, media, code comments,
documentation, or any digital or physical medium.
This clause does NOT prohibit legitimate criticism, bug reports, issue reports, or fair‑use commentary
regarding the Software. Malicious false statements intended to harm reputation are prohibited.

2. When distributing an open‑source derivative work based upon the Software,
there is no mandatory requirement to include the full text of this PNC License,
nor mandatory attribution to the original author. The distributor is not required
to carry copies of the original source files.

3. When distributing a closed‑source derivative work, the original author shall be
clearly acknowledged within accompanying documentation, including but not limited to
user manuals, readme files, and distribution notes. Such attribution shall be
reasonably discoverable by end‑users; it shall not be hidden in deep‑level file directories,
and shall appear in at least one of the software’s about screen, README document, or release notes.

4. No commercial activity may be carried out in the name of the original author
or the original project without prior explicit written consent. Written consent
includes signed physical documents, digitally signed electronic communications.
Oral consent shall not be deemed valid.

5. Modification quantification rules:
For the purpose of this License, the percentage‑based rules are contractual terms of this agreement,
and do NOT override statutory copyright law. Even if a file meets the 50% modification threshold,
if the work still constitutes substantial similarity to the original Software under applicable copyright law,
the original author retains all statutory copyright rights.

Counting shall be performed on a per‑file basis, against the original unmodified version
of the source file provided by the original author.

For each source file derived from the Software:
If modifications to the file exceed fifty percent (50%) of the file’s valid source lines,
such file shall be deemed independently authored code of the modifier under this License.
The modifier may apply any open‑source or proprietary license to such files, and no attribution to the
original author is required under this License.

If modifications to a source file are fifty percent (50%) or less of valid source lines,
the derivative work containing this file may only be distributed under the MIT License,
BSD 3‑Clause License, or this PNC License.

Aggregate code calculation rule:
The aggregate ratio is calculated as:
(total valid source lines of unmodified / partially‑modified original source files (modifications ≤ 50%))
DIVIDED BY
(total valid source lines of entire derivative codebase, including all third‑party library source code incorporated)

Any derivative work where this aggregate ratio is more than thirty percent (30%) shall
not be utilised, distributed, or operated for any Commercial activity as defined above.

The following activities are exempt from the commercial restriction set forth above:
official project promotion, and the creation and distribution of official development documentation.

Redistribution rule for binaries:
- Unmodified original binary builds of the Software: may be freely distributed via public online channels.
- Modified derivative binary builds of the Software: may NOT be redistributed via public online download channels
(mirror sites, third‑party app stores, public file hosting services) without prior written permission from original author.
Local compilation, personal offline packaging for private use, and internal team distribution
are not subject to this online‑distribution prohibition.

5‑A. Ratio Calculator Requirement
Any distributor exercising rights under this PNC License shall retain the complete source code
of the ratio‑calculation logic conforming to the base specification defined in Section 5.
The distributor may extend this calculator by adding additional metrics, custom rules, dead‑code detection logic,
or other supplementary functionality. However, the original base calculation logic of the calculator SHALL NOT
be removed, altered, or deleted. All extensions must be appended on top of the original base implementation.

In case of dispute, the result produced by the original author’s reference counting tool shall prevail.
Distributors are not required to bundle the calculator program inside every binary artifact;
the source code of the calculator logic must be available upon reasonable request for dispute resolution.

